      "object": "BMI and body image inflexibility are predictive of eating disorders symptoms."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:limites",
      "object": "All measures rely on self reports, they are somewhat prone to measurement error that arises from self report bias. BMI has some disadvantages; BMI is biased because this measure does not take into account the difference between muscle mass and fat mass. The participants comprise only universities students. This study focuses on body image distorsion as one of the predictors while other possible variables such as self compassion, perfectionism, and obsessive compulsive personality disorder were not considered. The cross sectional design does not allow the examination of causality and the direction of the pathways."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:perspectives",
      "object": "Our findings suggest that the prevention and treatment of exercise dependence symptoms should consider interventions to improve the indivdiuals attitude towards the perception of their own body by addressing body image inflexibility."
